{"_id":"6a2ff5342204ffbc59e5a5f8","roadmapSlug":"python-data-analysis","nodeId":"OwEBYI4u7nb9-UGOR9SQf","description":"# Excel\n\nExcel files (`.xlsx`, `.xls`) are loaded with `pd.read_excel()`, which supports selecting sheets, skipping rows, and reading specific columns. The `openpyxl` library is required for `.xlsx` files. Excel is common in business environments, and analysts frequently need to read and write it as part of reporting workflows.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"pandas.read_excel","url":"https://pandas.pydata.org/docs/reference/api/pandas.read_excel.html","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb42"},{"type":"article","title":"Pandas read_excel: Reading Excel Files in Python","url":"https://www.digitalocean.com/community/tutorials/pandas-read_excel-reading-excel-file-in-python","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb43"}],"createdAt":"2026-06-15T12:51:00.938Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-07T12:44:22.099Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e3360acf8c05faf5e1c2a","title":"DataCamp - Data Analyst with Python","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/QY0dY9"},{"_id":"6a5e3365acf8c05faf5e1ded","title":"DataCamp - Python Data Fundamentals","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/k4V24x"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/python-data-analysis/content/OwEBYI4u7nb9-UGOR9SQf.md"}